                  Excursion 2 – From the Sierra Nevada Mountains to the Badlands
                  of Guadix
                </p>
                <p class="">
                  After breakfast, we transfer to a traditional mountain village
                  near Granada, where today's cycling adventure begins. From
                  here, we ride along the northern slopes of the Sierra Nevada,
                  following quiet roads that wind through forests, mountain
                  valleys, and spectacular natural scenery.
                </p>
                <p class="">
                  The route follows the course of a mountain river towards the
                  famous Puerto de los Blancares, one of the classic mountain
                  passes of the region. Along the way, we stop at an impressive
                  dam. Continuing through the mountains, we enjoy a
                  well-deserved coffee break before reaching our picnic spot at
                  a panoramic viewpoint, where we can relax and take in the
                  scenery
                </p>
                <p class="">
                  During the second part of the ride, the landscape gradually
                  transforms. The green mountain forests begin to disappear,
                  giving way to a much drier and more rugged environment. Eroded
                  hills, dramatic rock formations, and wide-open spaces announce
                  our arrival in the unique Badlands of Granada, one of the most
                  striking landscapes in southern Spain.
                </p>
                <p class="">
                  Our route eventually leads us into the Guadix region, famous
                  for its extraordinary cave dwellings. For centuries, local
                  inhabitants have lived in homes carved directly into the soft
                  rock, creating one of the most distinctive architectural
                  landscapes in Europe.
                </p>
