                </p>
                <p class="">
                  Wander through Granada's historic centre, with its charming
                  streets, lively squares, and inviting cafés and terraces.
                  Sample local tapas, browse the markets, or explore the
                  enchanting Albaicín, the city's historic Arab quarter, famous
                  for its whitewashed houses, narrow winding streets, and
                  spectacular viewpoints overlooking Granada and the Sierra
                  Nevada.
                </p>
                <p class="">
                  A highlight of any visit to Granada is the world-famous
                  Alhambra, the magnificent Moorish palace and fortress complex
                  that dominates the city skyline. Its stunning architecture,
                  beautiful gardens, and rich history make it one of Spain's
                  most treasured landmarks. Please note: Entrance tickets for
                  the Alhambra are in very high demand and often need to be
                  booked several months in advance.
                </p>
                <p class="font-bold">Optional Suggestions</p>
                <p class="">
