                  Excursion 4 – Cycling Through the Gorafe Desert.
                </p>
                <p class="">
                  Today we discover one of Andalusia's most unexpected
                  landscapes: the spectacular Gorafe Desert. Located in the
                  heart of the Granada UNESCO Global Geopark, this extraordinary
                  region feels more like another continent than southern Spain.
                  Vast open spaces, dramatic canyons, dry riverbeds, rugged
                  badlands, and high plateaus create a landscape unlike anything
                  else on this tour.
                </p>
                <p class="">
                  Our route follows quiet roads through an ever-changing scenery
                  of red and ochre-coloured cliffs, striking rock formations,
                  deep ravines, and panoramic viewpoints. The landscape,
                  sculpted by millions of years of erosion, is often compared to
                  the canyon country of the American Southwest and offers some
                  of the most spectacular cycling terrain in Spain.
                </p>
                <p class="">
                  As we ride through this remarkable environment, we gain an
                  appreciation not only for its geological significance but also
                  for its rich human history. The Gorafe area is home to more
                  than 200 dolmens—prehistoric megalithic tombs dating back over
                  5,000 years—making it one of the largest concentrations of
                  prehistoric monuments in Europe.
                </p>
                <p class="">
                  This unique combination of dramatic scenery, geological
                  wonders, and ancient history makes today's ride a true
                  highlight of the tour.
                </p>
